<title>USA: Teva says FDA approves Cefaclor.</title>
<headline>Teva says FDA approves Cefaclor.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Teva Pharmaceutical Industries Ltd said on Wednesday it recieved U.S. Food and Drug Administration approval to manufacture and market its Cefaclor antibiotic capsules.  </p>
<p>Cefaclor was the generic equivalent of Eli Lilly and Co's Ceclor, Teva said in a statement.</p>
<p>There were already several Abbreviated New Drug Application (ANDA) approvals for generic versions of this product, Teva said.</p>
<p>The company was unavailable for comment about the potential market value of Cefaclor.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
